¶
{{smaller block|He was ''tricked'' out of the money while he was writing a receipt for it, and sent away without a farthing.
{{right|''Vanbrugh'', Journey to London, iv. 1.}}}}

2. To bring, render, or induce by trickery; beguile; inveigle; cajole.

{{smaller block|They were thus ''tricked'' of their present.
{{right|''Bacon'', Physical Fables, ii.}}}}
